# The rule applied here: ignore what a THOR run can rebuild, track what it
# cannot.  Size is the secondary consideration, not the primary one -- see the
# note on experiments/ at the bottom, which is kept precisely because it is
# irreproducible despite being small.

# --- rendered datasets ------------------------------------------------------
# 2.3 GB between them, and every one is a pure function of the generator plus a
# seed.  Rebuilding occlusion_ds4 is ~2 hours of THOR; that is the real cost of
# losing them, so keep backups outside git rather than assuming git has them.
#
# What makes them reproducible is that the generator is tracked and the scene
# lists, seeds, camera band and occlusion ceiling are all constants in
# build/sgg/build_occlusion_dataset.py.  If you change those, record the change in
# TASKS.md or the rebuild will not match.
# `datasets/*`, not `datasets/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, and the two exceptions below need to.
datasets/*

# ...except the robot experiments' scene lists.  512 KB of JSON holding no
# images -- THOR builds the room at run time -- and every number in this repo
# was measured against a specific one.  Regenerating with a different seed does
# not reproduce them, so by this file's own rule they are tracked.
!datasets/robot/
!datasets/robot/*.json

# The layout note itself is documentation, not data.
!datasets/README.md

# Predictions live outside this tree (../sgg_nvs/results/) but guard against a
# copy being dropped in here.
*_baseline/
*_results.json

# --- transfer archives ------------------------------------------------------
# These duplicate a directory that already exists; 1.9 GB of them accumulated
# once already before being cleaned out.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz

# --- tool output ------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerated on demand and never referenced by TASKS.md.
demo/
*/_viz/
*.mp4
*.avi

# Slurm writes these next to the job script so they are one `ls` away rather
# than off in /work; the script itself is tracked, its output is not.
slurm/logs/

# --- python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

# --- editor / os ------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# --- hidden-target scenarios ------------------------------------------------
# The renders are reproducible: build/sgg/build_hidden_target.py is seeded, so the
# same scene and seed rebuild the same scenario.  The scenario.json holding the
# poses, the occluder placement and the achieved occlusion is what you would
# actually cite, and the demo figure is a result -- both stay.
hidden_target/*/*.png
!hidden_target/*/scenario.json

# The remembered start poses of the interactive scene explorer that used to be
# `robot/drive_triplet_scene.py` -- a cache of a search whose result is
# reproducible from the dataset, not a record of anything.  The explorer is gone
# (its measurement half is `robot/task/measure.py`); the rule stays until the
# directory does.
.drive_poses/

# --- experiment output ------------------------------------------------------
# `results/` was `nvs_pilot/` until it stopped being either NVS-only or a pilot.
# Renders only.  A run stores 20 full-resolution synthesised views per case
# (~16 MB each), and every one of them is reproducible: cases.json fixes the
# scene, the start pose and the occluder type, and the sweep is deterministic
# given those.  What you would actually cite is results.json -- every pose,
# occlusion, rank and per-step trail is in it -- and the case list that
# generated it, so those two stay.
results/**/*.png
# Build logs are not tracked here.  A generator's log is the rejection trace of
# one run -- useful while tuning thresholds, superseded the next time the
# generator changes -- and what has to survive is the DECISION it drove, which
# belongs in the generator's own comments where it cannot drift from the code.
# `build/robot/build_slot.py`'s threshold notes are the worked example: the numbers that set
# --falloff and --max-landmark-ratio are in the source, not in build_slot.log.
# `experiments/build_logs/` is the deliberate exception below, and for the
# opposite reason: the datasets it describes are NOT tracked, so those logs are
# the only record of how they were built.
results/**/*.log
!results/**/results.json
!results/cases*.json
# Experiment results are the point of the runs, not build output: a few hundred
# KB of ranks and occlusions that cost a quarter of an hour of THOR and EGTR,
# and re-running is not bit-reproducible (GPU float order flips near-ties).
!results/fuse_live*.json
results/real/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DELIBERATELY TRACKED, despite looking like build output:
#
#   experiments/build_logs/   provenance for the datasets ignored above: the
#                             room families, scene x seed x view counts, camera
#                             band and per-scene yields each build ran with.
#   vg_prior.json             fitted on VG train, read at import by vg_gt.
#   vg_pair_prior.json        442 KB, fitted on 315642 VG relations.  Large for
#                             git, but rebuilding needs the Visual Genome dump,
#                             which is not part of this repo.
#
# Do not add them here on size grounds.
